      "predicate": "requires-agent-profile-permissions",
      "qualifier_status": "complete",
      "rationale": "The cloud-run section explicitly says cloud runs do not use Agent Profiles, but its failure checklist instructs readers to check profile command and MCP permissions. Both statements concern the same legacy cloud command; neither section supplies a configuration exception.",
      "rationale_class": "cloud-run-profile-scope-conflict",
      "reopened": false,
      "scope_quotes": [
        {
          "quote": "# Run Claude Code as a cloud agent, authenticating with a stored Anthropic secret\noz agent run-cloud \\\n  --environment <ENVIRONMENT_ID> \\\n  --harness claude \\\n  --claude-auth-secret ANTHROPIC_API_KEY \\\n  --prompt \"Review the latest PR and suggest fixes\"\n```\n\n**Key differences from `run`**\n\n* No `--cwd` \u2014 the environment determines the working directory.\n* No `--share` \u2014 sharing options are on `run`, not `run-cloud`.\n* No `--profile` \u2014 cloud runs do not use agent profiles.\n",
          "source": {
            "canonical_identity": "route:/agents/cli/oz-cli",
            "canonical_route": "/agents/cli/oz-cli",
            "content_sha256": "fe0853d907b75584aadaec00d222ec0ad5edc9c0b80eb45c028a7d75b70e6333",
            "heading": "Running agents remotely: \\`oz agent run-cloud\\`",
            "heading_anchor": "running-agents-remotely-oz-agent-run-cloud",
            "line_end": 291,
            "line_start": 278,
            "path": "src/content/docs/agents/cli/oz-cli/index.mdx",
            "repository": "warpdotdev/docs",
            "route": "/agents/cli/oz-cli/",
            "visibility": "public"
          }
        },
        {
          "quote": "#### Starting a run as an orchestration child\n\nThe `--parent-run-id` flag attaches the new run to an existing run as an [orchestration](/platform/orchestration/multi-agent-runs/) child. The child inherits the parent's lineage and scope, and it appears alongside the parent's other children instead of as a standalone run:\n\n```sh\noz agent run-cloud \\\n  --environment <ENVIRONMENT_ID> \\\n  --parent-run-id <PARENT_RUN_ID> \\\n  --title \"Backfill integration tests\" \\\n  --prompt \"Add integration tests for the new endpoints\"\n```\n\nPass the run ID of the run doing the spawning. Omit the flag for ordinary standalone runs.\n\n**When cloud runs fail**\n\n* Verify your environment has the correct repository and context.\n* Check that your profile allows the commands and MCP servers needed.\n* Ensure environment variables are set in the environment, not your local shell.\n",
          "source": {
            "canonical_identity": "route:/agents/cli/oz-cli",
            "canonical_route": "/agents/cli/oz-cli",
            "content_sha256": "fe0853d907b75584aadaec00d222ec0ad5edc9c0b80eb45c028a7d75b70e6333",
            "heading": "Starting a run as an orchestration child",
