      "qualifier_status": "complete",
      "rationale": "The split-architecture section explicitly says self-hosted code context routes through Warp in prompts and transcripts. The same deployment's selection guidance promises orchestration without sending code to Warp. The linked platform architecture also says code context transits Warp and may persist as run data, so the unrestricted selection promise conflicts with the documented boundary.",
      "rationale_class": "self-hosted-code-transit-scope-conflict",
      "reopened": false,
      "scope_quotes": [
        {
          "quote": "### Split architecture\n\nSelf-hosted deployments use a split architecture:\n\n* **Execution plane (customer-hosted)** - Source code repositories, build artifacts, shell commands, and runtime secrets stay on your infrastructure. Note that during agent interactions, code context is included in LLM prompts and session transcripts that route through Warp's servers under ZDR agreements (see [What transits Warp's servers](#what-transits-warps-servers)).\n* **Control plane (Warp-hosted)** - Task orchestration, observability data, and LLM inference route through Warp's servers under Zero Data Retention (ZDR) agreements.\n",
          "source": {
            "canonical_identity": "route:/enterprise/enterprise-features/architecture-and-deployment",
            "canonical_route": "/enterprise/enterprise-features/architecture-and-deployment",
            "content_sha256": "49a89792a39ba229f05c54700cfa91721cb36afc2a3fae0580011e6d61148df9",
            "heading": "Split architecture",
